---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { getPublishedSoftware } from "@/data/software";

const products = getPublishedSoftware();
const effective = "31 August 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use — BramLabs"
  description="Terms covering bramlabs.co, the BramLabs software products, and the original artwork published here."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1 class="h-page">Terms of Use</h1>
      <p class="doc-meta effective">Effective {effective}</p>

      <div class="prose">
        <p class="summary">
          Plain version: use the site and the products normally and nothing here
          will trouble you. Do not copy the artwork, do not attack the service,
          and understand that these are small tools offered as-is.
        </p>

        <h2>Who these terms are with</h2>
        <p>
          These terms are between you and BramLabs, an independent studio run by
          Bram. By using bramlabs.co or any BramLabs product, you agree to them.
          If you do not, stop using them.
        </p>

        <h2>The software products</h2>
        <p>
          Products distributed through a store —
          {
            products.map((p, i) => (
              <>
                {i > 0 && (i === products.length - 1 ? " and " : ", ")}
                <a href={`/software/${p.slug}/`}>{p.title}</a>
              </>
            ))
          }
          {" "}— are also subject to the terms of the platform they came from,
          such as the Chrome Web Store or the Amazon Appstore. Where a platform's
          terms conflict with these, the platform's terms govern the distribution
          and these govern everything else.
        </p>
        <p>
          Each product has its own <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>
          describing what it does with data. Those are part of these terms.
        </p>

        <h3>Acceptable use</h3>
        <p>You agree not to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Reverse engineer, decompile or redistribute a product except where law expressly permits it</li>
          <li>Use a product to break the law, or to breach the terms of any third-party service it interacts with</li>
          <li>Attack, overload or probe the service other than under the <a href="/security/">security policy</a></li>
          <li>Repackage a product and distribute it as your own, or ship it through unofficial mirrors</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Some products interact with third-party services that have their own
          rules. You are responsible for complying with those — using an
          extension does not transfer that responsibility to BramLabs.
        </p>

        <h2>Artwork and site content</h2>
        <p>
          The apparel graphics, illustrations, written content and design of this
          site are owned by BramLabs. You may look at them, link to them, and
          share links. You may not copy, redistribute, resell, or use them in
          your own products — printed or digital — without written permission.
        </p>
        <p>
          Product names and logos belonging to other companies are the property
          of those companies. Their appearance here is descriptive and does not
          imply endorsement or affiliation.
        </p>

        <h2>Availability and changes</h2>
        <p>
          These are small products maintained by one person. Features may change,
          and a product may be retired. If a product is retired, its support and
          privacy pages stay up for as long as anyone is plausibly still running
          it. Pages on this site may be updated without notice.
        </p>

        <h2>No warranty</h2>
        <p>
          The site and the products are provided "as is", without warranty of any
          kind, express or implied, including fitness for a particular purpose.
          BramLabs does not warrant that a product will be uninterrupted or
          error-free.
        </p>
        <p>
          Concretely: do not rely on any of these products as the sole record of
          something that matters — payroll hours, medication timing, a legal
          deadline. Keep your own record. Tools help; they are not a system of
          record.
        </p>

        <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the fullest extent permitted by law, BramLabs is not liable for
          indirect, incidental or consequential damages arising from use of the
          site or the products, including lost data, lost profits or missed
          shifts. Nothing here limits liability that cannot lawfully be limited —
          including liability for death or personal injury caused by negligence,
          or for fraud. Some jurisdictions do not allow certain exclusions, so
          parts of this section may not apply to you.
        </p>

        <h2>Governing law</h2>
        <p>
          These terms are governed by the law of the jurisdiction in which
          BramLabs operates, without regard to conflict-of-law rules. Nothing in
          this section removes a consumer protection you have in your own country
          of residence.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p>
          Material changes update the effective date at the top of this page.
          Continuing to use the site or the products afterwards means the revised
          terms apply. The current version took effect on {effective}.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these terms:
          <a href="mailto:contact@bramlabs.co">contact@bramlabs.co</a>
          <br />
          Product problems: the <a href="/feedback/">feedback form</a> or
          <a href="mailto:support@bramlabs.co">support@bramlabs.co</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style lang="scss">
  .effective {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--s-5);
  }

  .summary {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: var(--ink);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--ink);
    padding-left: var(--s-3);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
</style>
